-- Coastal barangays include near-shore water: each coastal polygon extends 500 m seaward from the
-- OpenStreetMap coastline (natural=coastline, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL). The water is split
-- from the shoreline itself (each 20 m of coast labelled with its barangay), so every border runs straight
-- out to sea from where it meets the shore; neighbouring towns' shores (Lugait, Linamon) keep their own
-- water. Unowned shore land joins the barangay it borders. Inland edges are unchanged.
-- Mirrors app/assets/iligan-barangays.json so map display and server matching agree.
